deepDives.body:
Every request resolves a principal with a `tenantId` from the session or token, never from the body. Repositories take `tenantId` as a required argument, so forgetting it is a type error. Underneath, each tenant-owned table has RLS:

```sql
ALTER TABLE documents ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE documents FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
CREATE POLICY tenant ON documents
  USING (tenant_id = current_setting('app.tenant_id')::uuid)
  WITH CHECK (tenant_id = current_setting('app.tenant_id')::uuid);
```

The app connects as a non-owner role and runs `SET LOCAL app.tenant_id` at the start of each transaction, so pooled connections never carry a stale tenant. Migrations and support tools use a separate role with audited access. The cross-tenant test suite calls every route with a second tenant's credentials and expects 404, and a separate test disables the application filter to prove RLS alone still blocks the read.
